# 4️⃣ Reverse an Array

## 📖 Definition

Reverse means arranging the elements in opposite order.

---

### Example

Before

```text
1 2 3 4 5
```

After

```text
5 4 3 2 1
```

---

### Two Pointer Approach

```
left = 0

right = n-1

Swap

Move left++

Move right--
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
#include<iostream>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
    int arr[] = {1,2,3,4,5};
    int n = 5;

    int left = 0;
    int right = n-1;

    while(left < right)
    {
        swap(arr[left],arr[right]);
        left++;
        right--;
    }

    for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
        cout<<arr[i]<<" ";
}
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

### Space Complexity

```
O(1)
```

