# 📊 Complexity Summary

| Problem | Time | Space |
|----------|------|-------|
| Find Maximum | O(n) | O(1) |
| Find Minimum | O(n) | O(1) |
| Largest & Second Largest | O(n) | O(1) |
| Reverse Array | O(n) | O(1) |
| Check Sorted Array | O(n) | O(1) |

---

# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Always solve these problems in **one traversal (O(n))** whenever possible.

✅ Use the **Two Pointer Technique** for reversing an array.

✅ Second Largest should be **distinct** from the largest element.

✅ Checking whether an array is sorted is often the first step before applying **Binary Search**.

---

# 📝 Summary

- Maximum and Minimum can be found in one traversal.
- Largest and Second Largest should be solved efficiently using two variables.
- Reverse an array using the Two Pointer approach.
- Checking if an array is sorted is a common prerequisite for many algorithms.
- All these problems can be solved in **O(n)** time with **O(1)** extra space.

